WEBVTT

00:03:57.765 --> 00:04:00.370
But of course, 
he looks at the front of it.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.278
He sees Xi-feng.

00:04:02.278 --> 00:04:03.878
His soul enters the mirror

00:04:03.878 --> 00:04:08.715
and he is dragged away 
in iron chains to die.

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:12.372
Not all Buddhists think this way
about romantic and erotic love,

00:04:12.372 --> 00:04:13.985
but the moral of this story

00:04:13.985 --> 00:04:17.045
is that such attachments
spell tragedy,

00:04:17.045 --> 00:04:20.901
and should, along with magic mirrors,
be avoided.

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:24.092
Love lets us reach beyond ourselves.

00:04:24.092 --> 00:04:26.899
Let's end on a slightly 
more positive note.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.048
The French philosopher Simone de Beauvoir


00:04:29.048 --> 00:04:32.934
proposed that love is the desire
to integrate with another